# WordPress Core Standards

- Keep feature logic in `inc/*.php`; keep templates minimal.
- Escape output by context: `esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`, `wp_kses`.
- Sanitize all user/config input before save or use.
- Add `defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit;` to PHP modules.
- Use existing text domain `imidzh` for translatable strings.
- Avoid direct SQL unless absolutely required and prepared.
- Do not add site-wide side effects on every request; use idempotent setup.

